class.description:
[TimerServer] owns all timers of the project. [Timer] nodes and [TimerInstance]s are timers of this server, identified by an [RID]. The server is ticked once per process and per physics frame by the [SceneTree] after all [code]_process[/code] callbacks, so a timer fires at the same point as a [SceneTreeTimer].
The server does not count down every timer each frame. It keeps eight clocks (idle or physics, pausable or always, scaled or unscaled), and a running timer stores only where it started on its clock. Each clock has one heap of event times (end, next tick, next alert). Per frame and clock the server compares the top of the heap with the clock, so a frame without events costs O(1) per clock regardless of how many timers run, and an event costs O(log N).
A timer is either a countdown or a stopwatch (see [enum TimerInfo.TimerTickMode]). The shown time is the time left for a countdown and the elapsed time for a stopwatch. Ticks and alerts are given in shown time.
Events reach the owner of a timer through one [Callable] (see [method timer_set_callback]), which receives the [enum TimerEvent] and the shown time. [Timer] and [TimerInstance] turn the events into signals. If the owner set with [method timer_set_object] is a [RefCounted], the server keeps it alive while the timer is running.
[b]Note:[/b] The server and its timers must only be used from the main thread.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _on_pause_menu_opened():
	TimerServer.pause_all()

func _on_pause_menu_closed():
	TimerServer.resume_all()

func start_cooldown():
	var info = TimerInfo.new()
	info.total_time = 90.0
	info.alerts = PackedFloat64Array([10.0])
	var timer = TimerServer.create_timer(info)
	timer.start()
	await timer.timeout
	print(TimerServer.format_time(90.0)) # Prints "01:30".
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
private void OnPauseMenuOpened()
{
	TimerServer.PauseAll();
}

private void OnPauseMenuClosed()
{
	TimerServer.ResumeAll();
}

private async void StartCooldown()
{
	var info = new TimerInfo();
	info.TotalTime = 90.0;
	info.Alerts = new double[] { 10.0 };
	TimerInstance timer = TimerServer.CreateTimer(info);
	timer.Start();
	await ToSignal(timer, TimerInstance.SignalName.Timeout);
	GD.Print(TimerServer.FormatTime(90.0)); // Prints "01:30".
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
